  "worked_solution": "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=5$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to grow as time increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250390/assets/546ca291c2419bc39cdc906fdc15318b912174347acf3987ae76cc6171c05d57.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
